# Access Control Policy

## Purpose

The purpose of this policy is to ensure that access to company information and systems is granted only to authorized users based on business requirements.

## Scope

This policy applies to:

- Employees
- Contractors
- Vendors
- Third-party users

## Policy Requirements

- Every user must have a unique account.
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) must be enabled for critical systems.
- Access shall follow the Principle of Least Privilege.
- Shared accounts are prohibited unless formally approved.
- User access shall be reviewed every quarter.
- Access must be removed immediately when an employee leaves the organization.

## Responsibilities

### IT Team

- Create user accounts
- Remove inactive accounts
- Perform quarterly access reviews

### Managers

- Approve access requests
- Review user permissions

### Employees

- Protect passwords
- Never share credentials

